# You should keep L0 — but demote it brutally

The existing pairwise machinery isn't useless.

Rename it.

### L0 — Preference probe

Measures:

`P(textual_selection | description, task, model)`

Allowed conclusions:

> “Under this forced-choice prompt, Llama X selected description A 82% of the time.”

Forbidden conclusion:

> “Agents are 82% more likely to use tools with property A.”

That sounds pedantic, but it is the difference between an actual scientific result and benchmark theatre.

L0 becomes extremely cheap **hypothesis generation**.

It does **not** enter the main evidence ledger as agent behavior.

