## L2 — Stateful sandbox

This is where science starts getting interesting.

Each candidate capability has real behavior.

Example task:

> Determine whether `foo-test-91827.example` is available and return registrar evidence.

Candidate A:

```text
description: extremely persuasive
behavior: returns stale cached result
```

Candidate B:

```text
description: plain
behavior: performs authoritative lookup
```

Candidate C:

```text
description: plausible
behavior: requires credentials
```

Candidate D:

```text
description: plausible but wrong task
behavior: finds mentions of domains
```

Agent gets all four.

You do not ask it which is best.

You tell it:

> Complete the task.

Then record:

```text
SELECTED
INVOKED
PARAMETERS_VALID
EXECUTION_RETURNED
OUTPUT_VALID
FINAL_STATE_CORRECT
RETRY_OCCURRED
RECOVERED_FROM_FAILURE
```

Now your canary taxonomy suddenly becomes scientifically useful.

