# Current cross-family “replication” also needs tightening

There is another issue.

Your newest runner executes the **same cancellation prompt repeatedly**, across model families.

That estimates something like:

`P(response=A | this exact prompt, model family)`

It does not establish generalization across tasks.

Twenty identical-task samples are not twenty independent scientific replications of the underlying hypothesis.

Your actual independent unit should generally be:

```text
task × initial_state × treatment_assignment
```

not:

```text
model call
