# Reliability matters independently of mean success

τ-bench's `pass^k` idea matters here. ([arXiv][2])

And 2026 work is pushing agent evaluation toward explicit reliability profiles rather than one accuracy number: repeated execution, perturbation robustness, fault tolerance and consistency. ([arXiv][7])

For every AgentSEOLab treatment calculate both:

```text
pass@1
```

Probability at least one attempt works — capability-ish.

and

```text
pass^k
```

Probability **all k attempts work** — reliability.

A tool description that changes:

```text
success 72% → 78%
```

but produces much less consistent behavior may be worse in an agent economy.

